IMPORT prelude

-- National Environment Agency Act 2002 (Singapore) -- the rules with decision content in a statutory-board Act: membership and
-- term (ss 5, 7), quorum and voting (s 9), approvals for companies and loans (ss 12(h), 23), the financial year (s 19), personal
-- immunity and the no-liability rule for public information services (s 17), the symbol offence (s 40), compensation for a
-- meteorological station (s 41), obstruction offences (s 42), auxiliary officers (s 42A), officers' liability (s 43), the
-- certificate-evidence notice (s 45), composition (s 46), secrecy (s 47) and the penalty cap for regulations (s 48(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NEAA2002.txt; the revised
-- edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021, and the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 7 of 2020 (s 23).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act, so SCOPED to the
-- provisions that decide something. Not encoded: the list of functions (s 11) and general powers (s 12) beyond s 12(h); the
-- common seal (s 4); committees and delegation (ss 14, 15); staff (s 16); estimates, grants, shares, accounts and investment
-- (ss 20-22, 24-27); the 2002 and 2007 transfers of property, staff and contracts (Part 6, ss 32-38A); jurisdiction (s 44);
-- references in other laws (s 49) and the Schedule. The offences in the environmental written laws themselves (EPMA, EPHA) are not
-- here; s 42 only borrows them.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Environment Agency Act 2002`

§§ `5 and 7 -- membership and term`

-- s 5(1): the Agency consists of "(a) a Chairperson; (b) a Deputy Chairperson; and (c) not less than 5 but not more than 12 other
-- members, all of whom must be appointed by the Minister". (2) "The Minister may appoint the chief executive to be a member."
-- s 7(1): a member holds office for "such term, not exceeding 3 years, as the Minister specifies"; (3) the Minister may revoke an
-- appointment "without giving any reason".
GIVEN `has a Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a Deputy Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency is constituted as s 5 requires` IF
        `has a Chairperson`
    AND `has a Deputy Chairperson`
    AND `number of other members` AT LEAST 5
    AND `number of other members` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `term in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is within s 7` IF
    `term in months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `term in months` AT MOST 36

§§ `9 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 9(1): "The quorum at every meeting of the Agency is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the total number of members
-- in office; (b) 4 members." [2/2012]. Compared without division: present x 3 >= members in office, and present >= 4.
-- (4) questions are "decided by a majority of votes of the members present and voting"; (5) the Chairperson or, in his or her
-- absence, the Deputy Chairperson "has a deliberative vote and, in the case of an equality of votes, he or she also has a casting
-- vote". INFERENCE: a member elected to preside under s 9(2) when both are absent has no casting vote, so a tie then fails.
GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
        `members present` AT LEAST 4
    AND `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members in office`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the Chairperson or Deputy presides` IS A BOOLEAN, `casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (    `votes for` EQUALS `votes against`
         AND `the Chairperson or Deputy presides`
         AND `casting vote is for`)

§§ `12(h) and 23 -- companies and loans`

-- s 12(h): the Agency may, "with the Minister's approval, form or participate in the formation of any company, partnership or
-- joint venture".
GIVEN `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may form a company or joint venture` IF `the Minister approved`

-- s 23(1): "The Agency cannot raise loans ... except in accordance with this section." (2)(c): by "debentures, bonds or any other
-- instrument as the Minister for Finance may approve". (3): "(a) from the Government; or (b) with the approval of the Minister for
-- Finance, from another source, whether within or outside Singapore." [7/2020]
GIVEN `lender is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister for Finance approved the source` IS A BOOLEAN, `raised by issuing an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister for Finance approved the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may raise the loan` IF
        (`lender is the Government` OR `Minister for Finance approved the source`)
    AND ((NOT `raised by issuing an instrument`) OR `Minister for Finance approved the instrument`)

§§ `19 -- financial year`

-- s 19: "The financial year of the Agency begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Returned as the calendar year in which the financial year begins.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year begins in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `17 -- immunity and public information`

-- s 17(1): no proceedings "shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Agency or other person acting under
-- the direction of the Agency for anything which is in good faith done ... in the execution or purported execution of this Act or
-- any other written law". (3): where the Agency supplies information to the public, neither it nor its employees are liable "for any
-- loss or damage ... by reason of any error or omission ... if made in good faith and in the ordinary course of the discharge of the
-- duties of such employees".
GIVEN `acted for the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution of this Act or any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is personally immune` IF
    `acted for the Agency` AND `acted in good faith` AND `in execution of this Act or any written law`

GIVEN `error in information supplied to the public` IS A BOOLEAN, `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency is not liable for the information error` IF
    `error in information supplied to the public` AND `made in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `40, 42, 47, 48 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 40(2): using a symbol "identical with that of the Agency, or which so resembles ... as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be
-- likely to" -- $10,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 42(2): (a) refusing access to, assaulting, obstructing, hindering or delaying an officer; (b) "wilfully misstates or without
-- lawful excuse refuses to give any information"; (c) failing to comply with a lawful demand -- $10,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 47(2): disclosure in breach of secrecy -- "$2,000 or ... 12 months or to both".
-- s 48(2): regulations may provide a fine up to $10,000 or 12 months or both, and for a continuing offence a further fine up to
-- $1,000 "for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using the Agency's symbol or a confusing imitation`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `wilfully misstating information to an officer`
    `failing to comply with an officer's lawful demand`
    `disclosing Agency information in breach of secrecy`
    `contravening regulations under s 48`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosing Agency information in breach of secrecy` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosing Agency information in breach of secrecy` THEN 12
    WHEN `contravening regulations under s 48` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a continuing regulation offence` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

GIVEN `identical to the symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
    `identical to the symbol` OR `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse`

-- s 42(2)(b): misstating must be WILFUL; refusing is an offence only "without lawful excuse".
GIVEN `wilfully misstated` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to give the information` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information offence is committed` IF
        `wilfully misstated`
    OR  (`refused to give the information` AND (NOT `had a lawful excuse`))

-- s 47(1): a person who "is or has been" a member, officer, employee, auxiliary officer or agent of the Agency, or a member of a
-- committee, must not disclose information obtained in that role, "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties
-- or the exercise of his or her functions or when lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the
-- provisions of any written law".
GIVEN `is or was within s 47(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained the information in that role` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed for duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN, `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure breaches s 47` IF
        `is or was within s 47(1)(a) or (b)`
    AND `obtained the information in that role`
    AND (NOT `disclosed for duties`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `41 -- meteorological station on private land`

-- s 41(1): in an emergency, where the chief executive is of the opinion that public health or safety may be adversely affected,
-- officers may enter land "after giving reasonable notice" to set up a meteorological observation station. (2) the Agency "must pay
-- compensation to the owner of the land for any permanent damage"; (4) "Except as provided in subsection (2), no action may be
-- brought against the Agency for any compensation".
GIVEN `the damage is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landowner is entitled to compensation` IF `the damage is permanent`

GIVEN `an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `chief executive thinks public health or safety may be affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `officers may enter the land` IF
    `an emergency` AND `chief executive thinks public health or safety may be affected` AND `reasonable notice given`

§§ `42A -- auxiliary officers`

-- s 42A(1): the chief executive must issue each auxiliary officer a written authorisation "specifying the powers ... that the
-- auxiliary officer may exercise, and no other powers". (2): the powers "may be exercised only to the extent authorised by the chief
-- executive ... and directed by an officer or employee of the Agency". (4): the authorisation may limit when, where and in what
-- circumstances. (7): the officer need not be "present at all times".
GIVEN `the power is in the written authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed by an Agency officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the authorised time, place and circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auxiliary officer may exercise the power` IF
    `the power is in the written authorisation` AND `directed by an Agency officer or employee` AND `within the authorised time, place and circumstances`

§§ `43 -- officers of bodies corporate`

-- s 43(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer
-- ... or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer", the officer "as well as the body corporate shall be guilty".
-- (3) and (4) say the same of partners and of officers or governing-body members of unincorporated associations.
GIVEN `the body committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the officer's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body committed an offence under this Act` AND (`with the officer's consent or connivance` OR `attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `45 -- certificate evidence`

-- s 45(3): a certificate "shall not be received in evidence ... unless the person charged has been given (a) a copy of the
-- certificate; and (b) notice of the intention of the prosecution to produce the certificate ... at least 10 clear days before the
-- commencement of the proceedings". Days are counted as day numbers; "clear days" is read as excluding both the day of service and
-- the day proceedings begin (an INFERENCE about the term, which the Act does not define).
GIVEN `service day` IS A NUMBER, `commencement day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clear days between` MEANS `commencement day` MINUS `service day` MINUS 1

GIVEN `copy given` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `service day` IS A NUMBER, `commencement day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is admissible` IF
        `copy given`
    AND `notice given`
    AND `the clear days between` `service day` `commencement day` AT LEAST 10

§§ `46 -- composition`

-- s 46(1): the chief executive or an authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum of money not exceeding $1,000". (2) on payment "no further proceedings are to be
-- taken"; (4) "All composition sums collected under this section must be paid into the Consolidated Fund" -- not to the Agency,
-- although s 21 sends "All moneys recovered or charges collected under this Act" to the Agency.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` GREATER THAN 0 AND `sum` AT MOST 1000

DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF `the Agency`, `the Consolidated Fund`

DECLARE Receipt IS ONE OF `a composition sum`, `a fee or charge collected under the Act`, `money recovered under the Act`

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt
GIVETH A Payee
`where the money goes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the receipt`
    WHEN `a composition sum` THEN `the Consolidated Fund`
    OTHERWISE `the Agency`
